      "id": 1,
      "text": "Grand Prairie began as Dechman in 1863 when Alexander McRae Dechman traded oxen and a broken wagon for 239 acres of land on the Trinity River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
