      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name changed to Grand Prairie after the U.S. Postal Service adopted the spelling “Deckman,” causing confusion with the railroad’s “Grand Prairie” designation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
